In the newly added API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the handler decrypts and parses the provided `keys` via:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

This `JSON.parse(...)` (and the preceding `symmetricDecrypt(...)`) is not wrapped in a `try/catch`. If the webhook payload has malformed JSON, invalid ciphertext, or a wrong/empty encryption key, this will throw and result in an unhandled exception (Next.js API route will return a 500) rather than a controlled 4xx response.

